// expect: 7
// SYNTAX §«Imports» — a module's IDENTITY is the module it resolves to,
// never the spelling that reached it. `lists` and `lib/lists` name one
// file, so importing the path-prefixed spelling from a module whose
// prelude already imported the bare one draws a SECOND edge to a module
// already in the DAG — and drawing an edge that exists is a no-op,
// because that is what an edge is.
//
// Born RED (2026-09-06): the DAG walk keyed its visited set by the
// SPELLING and resolved to a path on the next line, so the two spellings
// collected the same file twice and every declaration in it collided
// with itself — 58 diagnostics on this four-line program, while the
// identical source through the blob link is silent because the
// concatenation never resolves an import at all.
//
// That divergence is what this battery's manifest leg exists to catch,
// and it is the §11 tripwire-3 shape exactly: the wheel's own build is
// the cat-blob through stdin, and every lib spells its siblings bare, so
// no gate on the board had ever resolved a path-prefixed import.
import lib/lists

fn main() = len([1, 2, 3]) + 4
